#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0513 expect=noViolation domain=DM
#note "Authority: SDTM and SDTMIG Conformance Rules v2.0 CG0513 (Condition: ACTARMCD = null; Rule: ARMNRS ^= null). Row 1 is a treated subject with every arm variable populated. Rows 2-3 leave the actual (row 2) or all (row 3) arm variables empty and give the reason in ARMNRS (ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED / SCREEN FAILURE) -> no row fires."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DM class="SPECIAL PURPOSE" label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SUBJID   type=Char label="Subject Identifier for the Study"
col RFSTDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference Start Date/Time"
col RFENDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference End Date/Time"
col ARMCD    type=Char label="Planned Arm Code"
col ARM      type=Char label="Description of Planned Arm"
col ACTARMCD type=Char label="Actual Arm Code"
col ACTARM   type=Char label="Description of Actual Arm"
col ARMNRS   type=Char label="Reason Arm and/or Actual Arm is Null"
---
S1 | DM | S1-001 | 001 | 2024-01-10 | 2024-06-10 | PBO  | Placebo | PBO | Placebo |
S1 | DM | S1-002 | 002 |            |            | DRGA | Drug A  |     |         | ASSIGNED, NOT TREATED
S1 | DM | S1-003 | 003 |            |            |      |         |     |         | SCREEN FAILURE
